# *Three Forms of Meiosis for Translocation Heterozygote*

@body

![Slide image 6](assets/lect13d-meiosis_translocation/image_006.png)

- Spindles bind to closest centromeres
- 1+2 and 3+4 stay together

- Alternate
  - left binds to 1+4
  - right binds to 2+3
- Spindles have two possible choices

- Spindles bind to closest centromeres
- 1+3 and 2+4 stay together

=== layout: section

# Determine the Possible Gametes

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels
@replaceme

# *Rules of the Three Forms*

@left

- Numbers are arbitrary, but we'll stick with them to avoid confusion.
- Setup\:
  - [1\: transl.]{color=#FF00FF} with [red]{color=red} [centromere]{color=red}
  - 2\: normal with [blue centromere]{color=#0066FF}
  - 3\: normal with [red centromere]{color=red}
  - [4\: transl.]{color=#FF00FF} with [blue centromere]{color=#0066FF}
- Adjacent-1
  - [1]{color=#FF00FF} + 2 &#8596; 3 + [4]{color=#FF00FF}
- Adjacent-2
  - [1]{color=#FF00FF} + 3 &#8596; 2 + [4]{color=#FF00FF}
- Alternate
  - [1]{color=#FF00FF} + [4]{color=#FF00FF} &#8596; 2 + 3

@top-right

- Non-pairing\:
  - 1 does not share DNA with 4
  - 2 does not share DNA with 3
- Pairing\:
  - 1 pairs with 2 and 3
  - 2 pairs with 1 and 4
  - 3 pairs with 1 and 4
  - 4 pairs with 2 and 3

@bottom-right

![Slide image 7](assets/lect13d-meiosis_translocation/image_007.png)

