=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

- A phenotypically normal prospective couple seeks genetic counseling because the man knows that he has a translocation of a portion of his chromosome 4 that has been exchanged with a portion of his chromosome 12.
- Although his translocation is balanced, he and his wife want to know the probability that his sperm will be abnormal.
  - Assume that all gametes produce viable sperm, even if genetic material is missing
- What is your prognosis regarding his sperm?
  - A. None will carry the translocation.
  - B. 1/4 will be wildtype, 1/4 will have translocated chromosomes, and 1/2 will have both wildtype and translocated chromosomes.
  - C. 1/2 will be wildtype and 1/2 will have the translocation.
  - D. All will carry the same translocation as the father.

- [Answer\: B]{color=red}

- 4

- 12

- 4

- 4

- 12

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Rules of the Three Forms*

@body

- Situation\:
  - translocation of a portion of his chromosome 4 that has been exchanged with a portion of his chromosome 12.
  - translocation is balanced
- Setup\:
  - [1\: transl.]{color=#FF00FF} with [red centromere]{color=red}
  - 2\: normal with [blue centromere]{color=#0066FF}
  - 3\: normal with [red centromere]{color=red}
  - [4\: transl.]{color=#FF00FF} with [blue centromere]{color=#0066FF}
- Double check pairing system &#8594;

- Non-pairing\:
  - 1 does not share DNA with 4
  - 2 does not share DNA with 3
- Pairing\:
  - 1 pairs with 2 and 3
  - 2 pairs with 1 and 4
  - 3 pairs with 1 and 4
  - 4 pairs with 2 and 3

- 4

- 12

- 4

- 12

- 4

